# Android Clean Architecture Project Structure

This document outlines the complete directory structure and architecture of the Android Clean Architecture project, built with **Jetpack Compose** following **MVVM-Clean Architecture** principles.

## Project Root Structure

```
Android-Clean-Architecture/
├── build.gradle.kts                # Root build configuration
├── settings.gradle                 # Module inclusion settings
├── gradle.properties               # Project-wide properties
├── core-test/                      # Shared test utilities module
├── data/                           # Data layer module
├── domain/                         # Domain layer module
└── presentation/                   # Presentation layer module (App module)
```

## Main Application Structure

### Architecture Layers

#### 1. Domain Layer (`domain/`)

Contains business logic, entities, use cases, and repository interfaces. It is a pure Kotlin module with no Android dependencies.

```
domain/src/main/java/com/aliasadi/domain/
├── entities/                       # Business entities
│   └── MovieEntity.kt
├── repository/                     # Repository interfaces
│   └── MovieRepository.kt
├── usecase/                        # Business use cases
│   ├── GetMovieDetails.kt
│   ├── SearchMovies.kt
│   └── ...
└── util/                           # Domain utilities
    ├── DispatchersProvider.kt
    ├── NetworkMonitor.kt
    └── Result.kt
```

#### 2. Data Layer (`data/`)

Handles data persistence, repositories implementation, and external data sources (API/DB).

```
data/src/main/kotlin/com/aliasadi/data/
├── api/                            # Remote data sources (Retrofit)
│   └── MovieApi.kt
├── db/                             # Local database (Room)
│   ├── movies/                     # Movie related DB components
